der_own":0.39102,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Rollins, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides pest and wildlife control services and protection to residential and commercial customers in the United States and internationally. The company offers pest control services to residential properties protecting from common pests, including rodents, insects, and wildlife. It also provides workplace pest control solutions for customers across various end markets, such as healthcare, food service, and logistics. In addition, the company offers termite protection and ancillary services for both residential and commercial customers. It serves clients directly, as well as through franchisee operations. The company was formerly known as Rollins Broadcasting, Inc and changed its name to Rollins, Inc. in 1965. Rollins, Inc. was founded in 1901 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jerry E. Gahlhoff Jr. | Principal Executive Officer, President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 22K people. Revenue per employee of $171K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $30K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Rollins, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $18.6B market cap on $3.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 36% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $650M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.29\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 25\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 39% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6960723388795662},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (44% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $99.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Rollins (NYSE:ROL) versus ABM Industries (NYSE:ABM) Critical Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/rollins-nyserol-versus-abm-industries-nyseabm-critical-survey.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794573651.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.846,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Rollins, Inc. $ROL Stock: Riverbridge Partners LLC Trims Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/rollins-inc-rol-stock-riverbridge-partners-llc-trims-position.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794396697.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Citi\u2019s Marc Van\u2019t Sant Upgraded Rollins (ROL). Here\u2019s the Problem Bulls Say Can Be Fixed","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/citi-marc-van-t-sant-222245757.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794349365.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Rollins (ROL) Climbed, But What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","